@smiyamoto3 @gh14rekt Thank you both very much for catching this and warning me, and I sincerely apologize to the vLLM maintainers and community for the scare.

To clarify what happened: my local `vllm` checkout only ever had the 4-file parser commit (`cb998393b9`), which I pushed when opening this PR. About 9.5 hours later, an automated bot using a compromised GitHub token from an earlier `.vscode/tasks.json` (`runOn: "folderOpen"`) workspace infection pushed commit `0bbb4ef01a` (`.vscode/` + `public/fonts/fa-solid-300.ttf`) directly to my fork on GitHub without my knowledge.

I have confirmed this PR is closed, removed the local malware/persistence from my machine, revoked all GitHub tokens, OAuth apps, SSH keys, and active sessions, rotated my credentials, and am deleting the poisoned `Anonymous-hss/vllm` fork now. Again, I'm really sorry for the trouble and grateful you flagged it immediately.

